  "answer": "In a food chain, only a small proportion of the energy from one trophic level is transferred to the next. For example, when animals eat, only about 10% of their food is converted into new tissue, which becomes the food for the next level. The rest of the energy is used for life processes like respiration, or it is lost as waste. This means that the amount of energy decreases as we move up the food chain.",
